0..72 Comment "// The cumulative hierarchy as a W-type over the universe, after Aczel\'s"
73..149 Comment "// sets as well-founded trees and the HoTT book\'s §10.5. A set is a type of"
150..228 Comment "// members and a function picking each one: `Sup(a, f)` has the members `f(x)`"
229..305 Comment "// for `x : a`. The family occurs only to the right of the function\'s arrow,"
306..381 Comment "// so it is strictly positive, and it lives one universe above the types it"
382..459 Comment "// ranges over. A fold reaches each member through `f(x)` and recurses there,"
460..537 Comment "// one stage below the set; the codes these sets carry have no machine image,"
538..581 Comment "// so every item here checks and none runs."
583..611 Comment "// The type with no element."
612..618 Keyword "import"
619..620 StringLit "\""
620..639 StringLit "../data/empty.gandr"
639..640 StringLit "\""
640..641 Other ";"
